00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.890
[RETRO GAME BEEPING]

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.880
SPEAKER: Identity
Access Management

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.610
is how you can decide who does
what with your Google Cloud

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:10.780
resources.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.840
You can get incredibly specific
when you create an IAM policy,

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.540
but essentially you have
an identity, a role,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.950
and a resource.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.110
Cloud IAM is designed with a
clean, universal interface,

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.010
so you're able to manage
access across all Google Cloud

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.294
platform resources consistently,
from App Engine to GCE.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.710
In this hands-on
lab, you'll learn

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:31.780
how to assign a role
to a second user

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.180
and remove assigned roles
associated with identity

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.760
and access management, or IAM.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.580
During the lab, you'll sign in
with two different user names

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.520
to experience how granting
and revoking access

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.190
works from both the
viewer and owner role.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.320
Next up on our quest is
Kubernetes engine, Qwik Start.

